  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Grammar patterns matched over UniDic tokens. Each alternative is a sequence of steps; every field given in a step must match one token: surface (exact), base (orthographic base or lemma), pos (first part-of-speech level), form (conjugation form prefix). Shared rule data for the Python analyzer and a browser engine. Meanings are short learner notes, not dictionary glosses. An optional pattern-level \"after\" step must match the token just before the match: the connective て/で follows only a verb, adjective or auxiliary, so 僕でも is not 〜ても.",
